This file contains a discussion of most functions: its inputs, outputs,
side effects.  The idea is to codify what each function expects, what it
does, and what it returns, so its actual performance and usage elsewhere in
the code can be checked against this standard.  Some help functions are
left out.

****************************************************************************

SCAN.C:

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR fn2dir(char **pname,DIR *dir,int flag)

Inputs: *pname points to the start of the name string, including d:. dir
	points to an empty dir structure. flag is FN_NORM, FN_EARLY, or
	FN_DOTSOK.

Hidden inputs: run->p_curdrv, run->p_curdir

Outputs: If every component up to the last one is found, *pname is altered
	to point to the start of its own last component.  Returns E_OK and
	EFILNF if at least this much worked.  If E_OK, dir is fresh and
	contains the slot found.  If EFILNF, dir contains the drv and clust
	fields where the unsuccessful search started.  If FN_EARLY, the
	last component isn't even attempted, and dir is as for EFILNF. 
	Unless FN_DOTSOK, a last component of . or .. yields EBADRQ.
	Other errors (wildcards in path components) can yield EBADRQ.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR dir2dir(DIR *dir)

Inputs:	dir fields dev, recno, recoffs.

Outputs: dir is freshened: bcb and fcb are valid.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR dirfirst(DIR *dir,DMD *dmd) [macro]

Inputs:	dir fields dev and clust, and dmd.

Outputs: Other dir fields curcl, recno, recoffs are filled in, and dir2dir
	is called to fill in fcb and bcb.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR dirnext(DIR *dir, DMD *dmd) [macro/function]

Inputs: fresh dir (all fields but bcb); dmd

Outputs: fresh dir (all fields) which refers to the next slot in the
	dir, including jumping to the next record or cluster.  Returns
	nonzero for errors, including ERROR for hitting the end of the
	directory (in which case dir isn't fresh any more).

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR dirslot(DIR *dir)

Inputs: dir fields dev, clust only

Outputs: fresh dir (all fields) referring to the first available slot
	in the dir.  Extends the dir if necessary.  Returns ERROR if the
	dir is unexpandable (RD or disk full).

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR name2fcb(char *name,char *end,FCB *fcb)

Inputs: string at name, ending at end; if end is NULL, name ends at 0 byte.
	
Outputs: Fills name part of fcb with name.  Handles special cases "." and
	".." Returns EBADRQ on some illegal names - currently just "..a" -
	and doesn't touch fcb if name is illegal.  Handles wildcards.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

int wmatch(FCB *pat, FCB *fcb)

Inputs: Name and attr fields of FCB's.  

Outputs: Matches pat (possibly containing wildcards) against fcb.  Returns
	nonzero on a match, zero on mismatch. Attribute matching is here,
	too, including FA_LABEL.

****************************************************************************

FSHAND.C:

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

int sftprobe(): returns the index of the first available slot in sft, or -1.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

int syshnd(int h): returns the slot number in SFT for h, including indirect
	though run->p_uft if necessary.  Returns -NUMBIOS for errors, other
	negative numbers for BIOS devs.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR dfd_close(DFD *dfd): if the DFD is dirty, writes its info to the slot.
	Frees the DFD.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR ofd_close(OFD *ofd): frees the OFD.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

voidfn xmovs(int count, void *s, void *d): copy count bytes from s to d.
	

****************************************************************************

FSCL.C:

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

int buflist(int buftyp): turns buftyp into the index into bufl for that type.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

uint log2(uint n): returns log base 2 of n.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

voidfn flush(BCB *bcb)

Inputs:	valid, dirty buffer bcb

Actions: Writes all valid, dirty buffers on the same drive and list as bcb
	(including bcb itself) to disk, clearing their dirty bits.

Outputs: none

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

voidfn flushall(): writes all valid, dirty buffers to disk.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

usrio: used by xrw; flushes dirty buffers spanned by a r/w op, then does it.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

void *getrec(uint recn, DMD *dmd, int flag)

Inputs: recn, dmd, flag 0 (don't mark buffer dirty), 1 (mark dirty), or 2
	(mark dirty but don't actually read on a cache miss).

Outputs: a pointer to the first byte of a disk buffer for recn.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

uint getcl(uint cl,DMD *dmd): return the value of FAT entry for cl.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

voidfn clfix(uint cl,uint link, DMD *dmd): mark FAT entry for cl with link.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

uint nextcl(uint cl, DMD *dmd, int extflag, int *extended)

Inputs: cl, dmd, extflag.

Actions: Returns next cluster in chain. If extend and (EOF || !cl), links
	in a new cluster and sets *extend.

Outputs: next cluster or zero for error, *extended (nonzero if file extended).
	
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

uint fastcl(DMD *dmd,int freeflag)

Inputs: freeflag is zero to return the first free cluster, nonzero to
	return the number of free clusters.

Outputs: the first free cluster or the number of free clusters.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR xrw(int wrtflg, OFD *ofd, long len, void *ubufr, void (*bufxfr)())

Inputs: wrtflg zero for read, one for write.
	OFD fields o_bytnum, o_curcl, o_currec, o_curbyt.
	(If o_curcl is zero, currec and curbyt don't matter.)
	For reads, len should not exceed EOF.

Actions: performs I/O on the combination of cache buffers and records as
	appropriate.

Outputs: o_bytnum, o_curcl, o_currec, o_curbyt advanced appropriately.
	Assumes someone else will mark ofd->o_dfd dirty, so changes that
	to extend but doesn't mark it dirty.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR ckdrv(uint dev): build DMD for dev if necessary. Calls log() as a help.

****************************************************************************

FSFS.C:

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

DFD *getdfd(DIR *dir)

Inputs:	dir fields dev, dirrec, diroffs

Outputs: a DFD if one exists with matching dev, dirrec, diroffs; or NULL

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR ixcreat(char *name, int attr, DIR *dir)

Inputs: name, dir as for fn2dir; also attr

Actions: creates directory entry for name, with appropriate checks,
	including deleting existing files (again, with checks).

Outputs: fresh dir

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR ixopen(DIR *dir, int mode)

Inputs: fresh dir fields fcb, dev, clust, recno, recoffs

Outputs: ERR or a handle number referring to an OFD referring to a DFD for
the file at the slot specified by DIR.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

ERR ixdel(DIR *dir)

Inputs: fresh dir fields fcb, bcb, dev.

Actions: Mark dir slot with 0xe5, then free cluster chain

Outputs: un-fresh dir.


